@node LLM Stub
@section LLM Stub
@cindex llm_stub.py
@cindex LLM backends

@file{src/codebud/llm_stub.py} is the only module that talks to a model.
Its main function is @code{call_llm(prompt, timeout=600.0, on_chunk=None)};
it also provides @code{call_llm_plain()} (conversational fallback),
@code{summarize_conversation()} (@code{/compact}), @code{list_models()},
@code{warm_model_sync()}, @code{prewarm_model()}, @code{ModelHeartbeat},
@code{num_ctx()} and @code{ollama_proxies()}.

It selects a backend in this priority order:

@table @strong
@item ollama
(@env{CODEBUD_BACKEND} unset or @code{ollama}) --- needs
@env{OLLAMA_MODEL} and a server at @env{OLLAMA_BASE_URL} that responds to
@code{GET /api/tags}.  Uses @code{POST /api/generate} with
@code{stream=True}, @code{temperature=0} and the same @code{num_ctx} on
every request; HTTP proxies are bypassed for a local server.

@item openai
(@env{CODEBUD_BACKEND=openai} only) --- needs @env{OPENAI_API_KEY} and the
optional @code{codebud[openai]} extra.  Uses a non-streaming
@code{client.chat.completions.create()} call with @code{temperature=0}.
@end table

@noindent
There is no fallback between them.  When the chosen backend cannot be
used, @code{call_llm()} raises @code{LLMUnavailable} with the reason; the
planner returns it as @code{llm_unavailable}, which @code{AgentCore}
reports instead of attempting a chat reply.

The @code{on_chunk} callback receives each text fragment from the Ollama
streaming response.  The CLI passes @code{ProgressIndicator.on_chunk} here
to drive the live token counter without coupling display logic to the LLM
layer.


